## DESCRIPTION
## Determine which sets are vectors spaces from a list of choices.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Abstract vector spaces)
## DBsection(Definition and properties)
## Date(10/3/2014)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('vector spaces')

# updated 2022.10.30

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'parserCheckboxList.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

# First define a number of sets

$a1 = non_zero_random(-3, 3);
$a2 = non_zero_random(-3, 3);
$a3 = non_zero_random(-3, 3);
$a4 = non_zero_random(-3, 3);
$k  = random(3, 6);
$n  = random(1, 5);

$cb = CheckboxList(
    [ [
        'The set of vectors of the form \(\left\{ \left[ '
            . '\begin{array}{r} a \\ b \end{array} \right] t \; | \; '
            . 't \in \mathbb{R} \right\} \)',
        'The set of diagonal 2 by 2 matrices given by \( \left\{\left[ '
            . '\begin{array}{rr} a  & 0 \\ 0 & b \end{array} \right] \; | \;\; '
            . 'a, b \in \mathbb{R} \right\} \)',
        'The set of polynomials given by \( \left\{  ax^2 + (a+b)x + b  \; | \;\; '
            . 'a, b \in \mathbb{R} \right\} \)',
        '\(\mathbb{R}\)',
        "\(\mathbb{R}^{$k}\)",
        "The set of vectors of the form \(\left\{\left[ "
            . "\begin{array}{r} $a3 \\ $a4 \end{array} \right] + "
            . "\left[ \begin{array}{r} $a1 \\ $a2 \end{array} \right] t \; | \; "
            . "\;t \in \mathbb{R}\right\} \)",
        "The set of vectors of the form \(\left\{\left[ "
            . "\begin{array}{r} x_1 \\ x_2 \\ x_3 \end{array} \right]  \; | \; "
            . "x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = $n \right\}\)"
    ] ],
    [ 0 .. 4 ],
    labels    => 'abc',
    separator => '<div style="height: 2ex"></div>'
);

BEGIN_PGML
Select all sets that are vector spaces under the natural operations of addition and scalar multiplication.

[_]{$cb}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
One way to do this is to check all properties of vector spaces for each of these.  However, that takes a long time.  Some of the standard ways that a set fails being a vector space is that 
* The zero vector is not in the set.
* The vector addition results in a vector not in the set. 
* Scalar multiplication results in a vector not in the set.

Checking these, the solution is [$cb->correct_ans]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
